# Implementation Plan: DagsHub MLflow Tracking Integration

This document details the plan to integrate DagsHub hosted MLflow tracking into both subprojects (`1_MiniLM_V4_Model_On_Raw_Data_and_OFP_and_Canonical` and `2_MiniLM_Hybrid_FF_V4`).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> * **Zero-Dependency Core Integration:** The integration will support DagsHub in two ways:
>   1. **DagsHub Python Client:** If the `dagshub` python library is installed, the code will automatically use `dagshub.init(repo_owner, repo_name, mlflow=True)` to handle authentication and remote URI configuration.
>   2. **Manual Credentials Fallback:** If `dagshub` is not installed, the logger will set the `MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME` and `MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD` environment variables programmatically from the configuration settings, enabling standard HTTP Basic Authentication over HTTPS.
> * **Separation of Sanity & Production Configs:**
>   - **`test_config.yaml`:** Will continue to use `sqlite:///mlflow.db` to ensure that local verification runs (`run_e2e_verification.py`) remain completely offline, fast, and independent of remote network conditions or credential availability.
>   - **`4_config.yaml`:** Will receive new configuration parameters (`username`, `password`, `dagshub_repo`) for remote deployment.

